                                                "sense_id": "28cfee7b-e6af-3284-8701-041a0c968cbe",
                                                "text": "Reflecting on his long career chronicling scientists, J. G. Crowther wondered why it was that in the grand debates over the nature of light, x-rays, and cathode rays, the British opted for particles and the continentals for waves."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
